   Dear sirs,

   I have a question concerning REVTeX.

   REVTeX is the preferred way to submit papers to the journals of the
   APS. Unfortunately the current version seems to run only in the
   compatibility mode of LaTeX2e. This means, that writers have to write
   in the - in the meantime ancient - LaTeX209. We have now people at the
   institute who did never learn LaTeX209, so for them REVTeX is rather
   inconvenient. Are there plans for a more modern version of REVTeX?

